  "note": "P0 verifies signature FRAMING only -- these vectors pin the bytes an Ed25519 signature must cover, not any signature value.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "signed_dm_with_recipient",
      "note": "PRIORITY: the preimage is the PADDED encoding with ttl forced to 0, the signature field removed and IS_RSR cleared. All three mutate in flight, so none of them can be inside the signature.",
      "packet": {
        "version": 1,
        "msg_type": 17,
        "ttl": 7,
        "timestamp": 1700000000000,
        "sender_id": "0011223344556677",
        "recipient_id": "8899aabbccddeeff",
        "payload_hex": "7369676e656420626f6479",
        "signature_hex": "abababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababab",
        "route": null,
        "is_rsr": true
      },
      "preimage_hex": "",
      "derivation": "BitchatPacket.toBinaryDataForSigning() calls BinaryProtocol.encode(unsignedPacket) WITHOUT a padding argument, so the parameter takes its Swift default of true. Preimage here = encode({ttl:0, signature:nil, isRSR:false}, padding:true): the frame is 14+8+8+11 = 41 bytes, optimalBlockSize(41) = 256, so 215 bytes of 0xD7 follow. Signing the 41 unpadded bytes verifies against itself and fails against every real peer."
    },
    {
